WEBVTT

s1.1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:07.629
Symphony is proven in layers: a fast suite, vendor mocks with real agents, real infrastructure, and Tern.

s2.1
00:00:09.079 --> 00:00:12.727
The default suite has 1,353 tests.

s2.2
00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:16.066
It needs a real Redis, but no network and no model call.

s2.3
00:00:16.066 --> 00:00:20.876
It covers every API route, the daemon, the runner, the trackers and the merger.

s3.1
00:00:21.226 --> 00:00:26.148
The mocks copy six vendor APIs, and each is built from the vendor's published spec.

s3.2
00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:31.457
SOURCES.md pins each file with its source, its date and its sha256.

s3.3
00:00:31.457 --> 00:00:36.317
Every request is checked against the spec. One outside it gets the documented error.

s3.4
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:41.707
Five mocks answer 501 for an operation they do not serve. No mock invents data.

s3.5
00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:46.310
Authentication and webhook signatures work as each vendor documents them.

s4.1
00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.153
The mocked run starts Redis, the mocks, Symphony and the merger, on one machine.

s4.2
00:00:51.153 --> 00:00:55.088
The agents are real: the pinned omp, on Amazon Bedrock.

s4.3
00:00:55.088 --> 00:01:00.169
Four configurations cover Linear with Slack, GitHub with Discord, and the chat assistant.

s4.4
00:01:00.169 --> 00:01:03.721
Every check passed, with no request outside the GitHub spec.

s5.1
00:01:04.071 --> 00:01:08.400
In scenario 1, a webhook started the agent in 44 milliseconds.

s5.2
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.857
It opened a ready pull request in 18.8 seconds.

s5.3
00:01:11.857 --> 00:01:17.135
The merger merged it in 64.8 seconds, or 55.8 on GitHub.

s5.4
00:01:17.135 --> 00:01:23.119
Other scenarios covered two repositories, a read-only investigation, and sub-issues with evidence.

s5.5
00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:28.922
Then an agent answered an inline comment, and a retrospective opened a learnings pull request.

s6.1
00:01:29.272 --> 00:01:33.609
Scenario 7 opened a red main ticket in 2.3 seconds.

s6.2
00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:37.493
Scenario 8 sent a real bug back in 30.3 seconds.

s6.3
00:01:37.493 --> 00:01:41.277
The assistant answered on Slack and on Discord in about 10 seconds.

s6.4
00:01:41.277 --> 00:01:45.105
A mapped click created a ticket tree. An unmapped click was refused.

s6.5
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:49.323
Through the gateway, an MCP call never carried the agent's own token.

s6.6
00:01:49.323 --> 00:01:53.030
The run found seven defects. Each fix has a regression test.

s6.7
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:59.207
The mocks are not the vendors. Real rate limits, webhook retries and Kubernetes are not in this run.

s7.1
00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:04.889
The kind run deploys Symphony on a local Kubernetes cluster, and runs one real attempt.

s7.2
00:02:04.889 --> 00:02:09.607
From an empty machine to a deleted cluster, it took 275 seconds.

s7.3
00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:15.020
A ticket became a Job in 7.7 seconds, and the agent ran at 15.3.

s7.4
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.475
Live events reached the host in 3 milliseconds. A steer applied in 13.

s7.5
00:02:19.475 --> 00:02:22.588
A refresh resumed the same session, on the same pod.

s7.6
00:02:22.588 --> 00:02:26.842
Its limits: the memory tracker, one turn per attempt, and no merger.

s8.1
00:02:27.192 --> 00:02:32.910
The merger certification uses a real GitHub repository, real CI and real agents.

s8.2
00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.982
A clean merge, a sent-back bug and a batch passed. A conflict passed on the third round.

s8.3
00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:42.120
A batch on a protected main failed first. After the fix, it passed.

s8.4
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.713
With no findings, a review took 10 to 40 seconds. Eight bugs were fixed.

s8.5
00:02:46.713 --> 00:02:51.844
Its limits: a user token, not a GitHub App, no webhooks, and a recorded tracker and chat.

s8.6
00:02:51.844 --> 00:02:55.493
Main stayed green, so the main watch opened no ticket there.

s9.1
00:02:55.843 --> 00:03:00.932
Tern's 37 tests run a real Tern server, headless, with the plugin as a fixture.

s9.2
00:03:00.932 --> 00:03:06.990
One suite uses a fake API. The other uses Redis, the real API and the real CLI.

s9.3
00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.363
A test fails if Tern logs a plugin error.

s9.4
00:03:09.363 --> 00:03:12.720
The same harness renders the screenshots in the docs.
